  "question": {
    "text": "A charged particle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math> is placed at the centre <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></em> of a cube of length <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></em> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>ABCDEFGH</mi></mfenced></math>. Another same charge <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></math></em> is placed at a distance <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> </em>from <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>.</em>&nbsp;If the total electric flux through the cube is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>ϕ</mi></math>&nbsp;then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ϕ</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0002_245948710359.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 313px;\" />"
  },
